VoodooI2C: VoodooI2C/VoodooI2C at 5c0c99cc451b03790c684ce6552c3f61620ad46b.
Its GPLv3 license and original copyrights are retained in corresponding source.
The Samsung matching patch and build packaging modifications are marked experimental.

VoodooGPIO: VoodooI2C/VoodooGPIO at 733dc8063f5ef07288a7bc648fff5348df6d8f65.
Its original GPLv3 LICENSE.md and copyright notices remain intact.
An independently authored GPL-3.0-only Samsung GPI1 class and bounded ACPI
resource-source reader are added alongside the unchanged upstream platform
classes. The experimental personality is disabled by default. GPIO and HID
function on the Samsung target have not been established.
Linux pinctrl-intel-platform/pinctrl-intel at
e5f0a698b34ed76002dc5cff3804a61c80233a7a were inspected as GPL-2.0 references
for hardware/property semantics. No Linux implementation is copied into this
repository, its generated GPIO patch or its corresponding-source package.

VoodooI2CHID: VoodooI2C/VoodooI2CHID at 27277936bc16c215ae7f9b31e76e3231778d04bd.
It is an upstream satellite of the GPLv3 VoodooI2C project. Original source
and copyright notices remain intact.

VoodooInput: acidanthera/VoodooInput at d897813718c2ef9ad143b6a86240fe52dcb1693e.
This separately built, unchanged upstream input component retains its GPLv2
LICENSE.txt. It is not relicensed as GPLv3. Its interface headers remain
in the corresponding upstream source tree with their original notices.

MacKernelSDK: external Apple kernel SDK dependency at
3f750085caa17ec3a7880f11c11bf4f48cd6a164 in acidanthera/MacKernelSDK.
Its headers and libkmod retain their original Apple licenses. They are not
LunarBridge code and are not relicensed or copied into this repository.
The build links SDK Library/x86_64/libkmod.a, SHA-256
7a751671bbe96c9c7b5416078df600b768c00c0dc5178d8acd8f52539c7ccd4e.
The experimental package includes SDK LICENSE.txt (Apple Public Source
License 2.0), original README, available Library/kmod source and a dedicated
SOURCE-NOTICES-SDK.txt. The prebuilt library has not been rebuilt from
these sources and compared byte-for-byte; no such proof is claimed.

Corresponding upstream source, original license texts, build scripts, pins
and source hashes accompany the experimental I2C build package. A successful
CI build is not a macOS Tahoe load, hardware, GPIO/HID or Secure Boot test.
